# Spes

Private Chrome and microsoft edge extension (Manifest V3) for two users only — not a public product. Tracks job applications together.

## Stack

- Manifest V3, TypeScript
- React for popup and options UI
- Firebase Auth + Firestore as the shared backend
- Google Gemini API for job-info extraction and CV / cover-letter generation
- Vite for the extension bundle

## Two-user privacy

- Each user signs in with Firebase Auth (Google sign-in is fine).
- Each user has a private `applications` collection. Do not expose one user's application details to the other.
- Both users can read a shared `streaks` document/collection so they can see each other's activity only.

## Data model

- `applications/{uid}/items/{appId}`: `title`, `company`, `url`, `description`, `status` (`to-apply` | `applied` | `interview` | `rejected` | `offer`), `dueDate` (nullable), `notes`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `cvVersionUsed` (optional), `coverLetterVersionUsed` (optional)
- `streaks/{uid}`: `currentStreak`, `lastActivityDate`, `applicationsThisWeek`
- `profiles/{uid}`: `baseCV`, `reusableBullets`, `displayName`, `rawDump`, `structuredFields` (`fullName`, `email`, `phone`, `address` `{street, city, stateProvince, postalCode, country}`, `linkedinUrl`, `portfolioUrl`, `workAuthorization`, `yearsExperience`, `salaryExpectation`, `noticePeriod`, `eeoAnswers`, `customFields`), `lastParsedFromDump` (ISO string or null)

## Product rules

- Never auto-save data extracted from a webpage without the user reviewing it first in a form. Extraction is a suggestion, not a commit.
- Keep the UI minimal and fast. Favor working functionality over visual polish at this stage.
